+# M10.5 · Signed return of one spectroscopy excitation
+
+$$
+L=D-A,\quad M=2F-D-A,\quad H_\kappa=\kappa M/2,\quad
+b=(|u\rangle-|v\rangle)/\sqrt{2},\quad E=|b\rangle\langle b|/8 .
+$$
+
+On accessible joint histories, $A$ joins a load hop and the corresponding reversal of one seam record, $D_{ii}=\sum_j A_{ij}$ and $F_{ii}=6-d_i$ uses the physical degree at the terminal port. An overall energy shift drops out of the detector probabilities. For each of the earlier donor's two spatial words, the tips reach ports 9 and 11 with a distinct common prefix. Integer multiplication gives $Mb=Lb=b$. At any freely chosen exposure $U_t^\dagger E U_t=E$. Thus each launch click probability $p$ predicts the same later click rate and a lower bound $8p$ on the probability of a two-tip reading on a fresh copy. [Physical graph construction](../scripts/m10_5_spectroscopy.py#L25) · [Joint selector and integer identities](../scripts/m10_5_spectroscopy.py#L52) · [Published native detector](https://github.com/FloatingPragma/observer-patch-holography/blob/9ade2801a7d0b5ebe16a9fc01923b93926246833/model/candidate_laws/interval_echo/openwave/row_04_spectral/phase_reader.py#L18)
+
+The material and both spatial words were selected for a frequency-and-wavelength experiment. Its pilot knew the spectrum. It checked every primary overlap, including the zero mode, and archived a later staggered alternative. Applying its primary rule to all three original arrow orders admits only the ascending two-dimensional match at energy 4 and squared wave number 1. The reversed-local material has no primary match in 2,730 histories, and the descending material gives only the parked zero mode. Reusing the donor for persistence was retrospective. The eleven writes around the earlier pair still have their original, target-aware provenance. [Original donor protocol](https://github.com/FloatingPragma/observer-patch-holography/blob/44f7680df55b4e68b89c301896df3e10237f046d/model/candidate_laws/interval_echo/openwave/row_30_selective/PROTOCOL.md) · [Earlier decision](m10_4_maintainer_review.md)
+
+The rising-fringe contact meter observes $\sin^2(|\kappa|t/2)$ on twelve appointments. It supplies a magnitude for pulse timing independently of the signed reader. At the sixteen resolved signed strengths run both archived pulses from the port-zero load. Zero supplies no resolved clock. The cap of 96 and 631 fair contacts give an original-start commissioning loss of $1-(1-2^{-96})^{631}$. On the same prepared object, sharp dephasing limits its signed weight to one half. A diagonal rate-matched swap process has the same bound. Switching the phase at just one tip tests readout sensitivity with both site populations fixed. [Clock inversion](../scripts/m10_5_spectroscopy.py#L79) · [Pulse, flight and comparison](../scripts/m10_5_spectroscopy.py#L97)
+
+| Comparison | Gate | Known author result |
+| --- | --- | --- |
+| Minimum native signed weight $8p$ | Above 0.98 | 0.999999500949, or 0.999999498949 after the declared numerical allowance. The minimum raw click is 0.124999937619. |
+| Launch counts through the identity | Simultaneous 99% lower bound above 0.98 | Above 0.99419. This uses simulated launch counts. The terminal banks are calculated probabilities. |
+| Four flight appointments | Absolute weight change below $2\times10^{-10}$ | All 32 preparations pass at 1, 7, 37 and 150 exchange-time units. |
+| Rate-matched swaps | Signed weight below 0.98 at 37 | Maximum 0.410439 across all four appointments. |
+
+**Adversarial check.** A separate calculation using spectral propagation obtained a minimum raw click of 0.124999937619 and a maximum phase-flipped raw click below $2.33\times10^{-9}$. On the same accessible graph, every mode of $4L$ passes the spectroscopic rule. Its first positive mode places only 0.366308 probability on even its two most occupied ports. This challenges the inference from selection to spatial confinement. The two enrolled signed modes persist under $4L$ as well. The rate-matched swap is one same-object changed-law comparison. The author preflight uses Python 3.12.6, NumPy 2.3.5 and SciPy 1.18.1. It imports standard Python, NumPy and SciPy only. From the OpenWave checkout run the following with an OPH checkout containing the three hashes in the task.
+
+~~~sh
+OPENBLAS_NUM_THREADS=1 OMP_NUM_THREADS=1 VECLIB_MAXIMUM_THREADS=1 \
+python -B -W error openwave/xperiments/m10_oph/research/scripts/m10_5_spectroscopy.py /path/to/oph
+~~~
+
+**Coherent changed-law comparison.** Port 9 has physical degree five and one blank degree reference. Remove that single reference during free flight on all six eligible joint histories. The Hamiltonian becomes $H'_\kappa=H_\kappa-\kappa P_9$ up to the common energy. Each launch retains its original coherent wavefunction and the two readouts agree at exposure zero. For either ideal signed ray the changed generator has energy variance $\kappa^2/4$. At exposure 37 all 32 original-start signed weights lie between 0.0218828 and 0.514994. Even the phase-insensitive two-port probability lies between 0.414087 and 0.744750. Both fall below the 0.98 gate on every preparation. The check is a target-aware perturbation of the flight law. [Control driver](../scripts/m10_5_reference_control.py) · [All altered and original readings](../data/m10_5_reference_control.json)
+
+~~~sh
+OPENBLAS_NUM_THREADS=1 OMP_NUM_THREADS=1 VECLIB_MAXIMUM_THREADS=1 \
+python -B -W error openwave/xperiments/m10_oph/research/scripts/m10_5_reference_control.py /path/to/oph \
+  --headline openwave/xperiments/m10_oph/research/scripts/m10_5_spectroscopy.py \
+  --check openwave/xperiments/m10_oph/research/data/m10_5_reference_control.json
+~~~
+
+The attached JSON is a local author preflight, before this proposed task was filed. The registered run and maintainer decision are outstanding. The public pair replay shows the M10.4 ancestor's home probability under eleven writes. [Preflight receipt](../data/m10_5_author_preflight.json) · [Task and input hashes](../tasks/m10_5_task_details.md) · [Pair replay](https://floatingpragma.ai/oph/simulation/openwave/row-4/)
